{"name":"Zucchini Flower","hex":"#e8a64e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zucchini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A courgette; a variety of squash, Cucurbita pepo, which bears edible fruit.","The edible fruit of this variety of squash."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of zucchino"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zucchini"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squash blossom","blocks":[{"text":"Squash blossoms are the edible flowers of Cucurbita species, particularly Cucurbita pepo, the species that produces zucchini (courgette), marrow, spaghetti squash, and many other types of squash."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Zucchini_flowers_-_stierch.jpg/330px-Zucchini_flowers_-_stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squash_blossom","wikidata":"Q42293042"},{"title":"Zucchini","blocks":[{"text":"Zucchini, courgette, or Cucurbita pepo var. cylindrica is a summer squash, a vining herbaceous plant whose fruit are harvested when their immature seeds and epicarp (rind) are still soft and edible. It is closely related, but not identical, to the marrow; its fruit may be called marrow when mature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg/330px-CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini","wikidata":"Q7533"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg/500px-Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg/1280px-Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg/500px-Kabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stuffed squash blossoms","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKabak_%C3%A7i%C3%A7e%C4%9Fi_dolma.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Kolokythoanthoi_gemistoi_me_giaourti.jpg/250px-Kolokythoanthoi_gemistoi_me_giaourti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/K